    {
      "id": "fHXrhCaglqRBHaTiLMa8b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2072.217376104985,
      "y": 3488.12425716014,
      "width": 1768.954833984375,
      "height": 770,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 593374598,
      "version": 1034,
      "versionNonce": 1027605446,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778323475263,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Digital Library -- College library where students can issue or return certain books \n\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n\n1. Capability to add a student in the library (CRUD)\n2. Librarians / Admins should be able to add or remove any book from the library \n3. Students should be able to place an order / request for an issuance or return of a given book\n4. Place fine for students who are returning the book after the due date. \n\n\nAssumptions:\n1. Student can issue the book for 'n' days free of cost\n2. Book can be issued for only 'n' number of days, after that there will be a certain fine each day that the student has to incur\n3. One order can consist of exactly 1 product only\n4. At any given point, a student cannot issue more than 3 books (and this is configurable)\n5. Every book is written by exactly 1 author but 1 author can write multiple books.\n\n \n\n\nRealme SmartPhone 'X' ==> Product",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Digital Library -- College library where students can issue or return certain books \n\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n\n1. Capability to add a student in the library (CRUD)\n2. Librarians / Admins should be able to add or remove any book from the library \n3. Students should be able to place an order / request for an issuance or return of a given book\n4. Place fine for students who are returning the book after the due date. \n\n\nAssumptions:\n1. Student can issue the book for 'n' days free of cost\n2. Book can be issued for only 'n' number of days, after that there will be a certain fine each day that the student has to incur\n3. One order can consist of exactly 1 product only\n4. At any given point, a student cannot issue more than 3 books (and this is configurable)\n5. Every book is written by exactly 1 author but 1 author can write multiple books.\n\n \n\n\nRealme SmartPhone 'X' ==> Product",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "bIWBGhyDmkkGvYgh3s9yn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4068.5517384440936,
      "y": 3688.0008284707606,
      "width": 773.8078002929688,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
